# Where the @fmmenchi packages come from: GitHub Packages, not npmjs — the docs plugin
# (ADR 0002). The mapping is SCOPED on purpose: a bare `registry=` line would send every
# dependency there.
#
# The token is deliberately not here: pnpm does not expand environment variables in
# credentials read from a project .npmrc. It comes from a source pnpm trusts:
#
#   in CI     the shared-platform `setup` brick, given `github-token` + `registry-url`
#             (actions/setup-node then writes the auth line into a USER-level npmrc)
#   locally   your own ~/.npmrc, once per machine:
#               pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" <a PAT with read:packages>
@fmmenchi:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
